so first of all congratulations on your  new single this is your first  solo single called even the stars what  can you tell us about the song what's it  all about  um well i think the song and the reason  i was  so excited about it to begin with is  it's just a very aspirational song and  it feels like it just  fits in with the time that we're in and  sort of stating that  there are peaks and valleys and that's  just a part of life and  you know you need the dark times to  really appreciate the light and that's  something that i've always  um i've always believed and um  you know with my own ups and downs in  life and whatever that may be  that's always something i keep in mind  so yeah that's kind of what the song  encompasses i would say  now is this a song you've been working  on for a little bit was it during this  time how did it all kind of come about  um so rock mafia um who wrote  a queen of mean for me from the  descendants movies um  they actually approached me after the  surprising success of queen of mean  because it really it really kind of took  off and  i was so grateful and they approached me  and asked if i wanted to work together  again and  i mean they're so talented and they've  worked with so many incredible people i  just  was like yes obviously um so  they presented me with some songs and  i gravitated towards even the stars and  you know we worked to  make it fit my voice and you know they  were just really accommodating and um  yeah i i just i i loved it and  we we recorded it back in november so it  was some time ago  um but obviously the pandemic  happened and it kind of put things on  hold so  uh it's finally here it's been i feel  like i've been sitting on it for a while  but  i'm just happy to be able to share it  yeah now the music video dropped friday  what was it like for you shooting that  video because obviously there's a lot of  restrictions when it comes to filming  right now so what was it like kind of  shooting a music video under new  guidelines  so odd i mean i have actually shot i've  shot a couple music videos but  um this was definitely well first of all  it was  it was a much more intimate sort of  smaller scale  um especially compared to when i shot  queen of mean for  descendants which wasn't really a music  video but you know what i mean still a  musical number  um and it was just it was wild like  i think it's going to be quite an  adjustment for hollywood coming back  into  filming and and getting productions up  and running again it's just  so many safety protocols and you just  want to make sure everyone  feels safe um  and i i felt safe i know the crew did  felt safe and they did such an amazing  job  like face shield masks keeping six feet  apart the whole time it was like it's  pretty  pretty crazy but yeah definitely  interesting well the music video is just  so beautiful  how did you come up with the concept for  it and i absolutely loved your very  colorful shiny jacket  you like a multi-colored jacket i'm like  i want that right  that's my favorite look for sure that  you have so fun  um so we actually had  an entirely different concept pre-coded  yeah the director millicent hales who  did a such a fantastic job she actually  directed me through zoom  for um the music video she had this  this whole treatment planned and it was  kind of bigger and like we were gonna  have  dancers and such and then you know that  kind of got shelved and then she came  back with this  sort of revised idea that was a little  more simplified but i honestly think it  ended up fitting the song  so well um and it was just like we  wanted to keep it airy  and aspirational and kind of dreamy  um yeah which i i think i think we  achieved you know  like  just being outside and in nature  uh it definitely succeeded it was just  it was very whimsical too had like a  really beautiful feeling to it  yeah nice yeah now you said on instagram  that music's always been a source of  light for you so do you feel like you're  writing music especially kind of during  this challenging time when all of us are  at home right now are you getting some  inspiration  definitely i feel i mean i obviously  have  we all have so much time um right now  more than  for myself at least than i'm used to  yeah so  i have been writing a lot i love writing  poetry which i hope to turn into lyrics  um  and also writing uh  writing some songs and seeing where that  goes and hoping that i can take those  back to  um the team at rock mafia and see what  we can do with them but yeah  just trying to stay creative um because  that's  that gives me energy and such a big part  of my  life um yeah yeah i think it's important  during the time  now are you listening to some of your  favorite artists as well to kind of get  through some of the more challenging  days like who are your favorite artists  to listen to  right now oh gosh so many different ones  i  i right now i'm loving the band litany  they're kind of an alt  pop band um if you haven't heard of them  i would  definitely recommend them um and then  a lot of different rappers there's this  new upcoming rapper bibi no money who i  love  um canadian as well nice  yeah and i i'm kind of like i guess all  over the map like  selena i always play her when i'm just  like  getting ready or something um  rain on me it's like constantly blasting  i feel like  and i also like led zeppelin like i love  i love led zeppelin so  those are great that's great artist  great music i love it  it is it's a good variety mix yeah yeah  um is there an artist that you would  just absolutely  it would be a dream come true to be able  to collaborate with  yes i mean again i feel like there's so  many talented people out there i would  just like  just love to work with um just came to  mind now actually i feel like megan the  stallion would be so fun to work with  so cool it's so rad and so fun  and um yeah i just think she's awesome  and so that would be awesome but also uh  jennifer lopez like  i worked with her on a tv show so i  worked with her in that capacity but  doing music with her  would be a dream come true for sure  right so you played her daughter on  shades of blue right  yes so would you say that you know with  jennifer lopez being like  the dominating factor when it comes to  music when it comes to dance would that  be kind of like a career that would just  be a dream come true for you  absolutely i think she does everything  so well and she's so talented  and gifted in sort of every region  um and she's just like she's  her work ethic is like nothing i've ever  seen before so definitely inspiring and  you know when i was working with her i  was definitely taking notes yeah  um well obviously i want to talk to you  about charms  um the show has such an amazing  following  people are loving it um how much fun is  it for you being able to play a  character that's such a strong role  model for men and women out there  i mean it's it's it's all i could really  hope for you know i hope to do projects  that really  make a difference in someone's life  resonates and i hope  people see themselves on screen um and  you know being biracial i i feel very  lucky to be at  you know the forefront of a show with  two other women of color um  so that that for me is like like that's  peak like that's that's what i've always  wanted um  and then i just i love my character  maggie because she's  she's girly and she loves fashion but  she's also just  really smart and caring and empathetic  and i think  it's important to realize you can be  both of those like they're not mutually  exclusive i think there's this  misconception where like you  you love makeup and you love fashion so  you're  i don't know i don't know less  intelligent i don't know why that's the  conception  but um but no you can be you can be  multiple things and that's kind of what  maggie is  i love that um so do you miss your  co-stars do you miss kind of being on  set with everybody  i do i i mean i see them more than i see  my  my own family really so they're they are  my second family and i really miss them  and i'm very excited to get back to work  um  yeah we're all kind of like scattered  all over the place so i haven't seen  them at all but  yeah very excited all right so you're  like a massive triple threat here  actress  singer dancer if you had to pick one  that you just connect with the most  that's hard i know this is a hard  question but  which one do you think you really  connect with the most  um you know i  would have said dancing  um years ago i that would have been my  pick for sure it's just i've  i started when i was three and it's also  it's always just been home for me but  um i would say now acting it's like  it's just it's just my life like i just  i give myself to my acting and  um yeah i don't i don't see  oh i can't see myself not doing it
 

